Principles

## Six rules every screen follows

### Glanceable first

One big number per card, a small dim label under it. Readable in a second while walking past.

### Calm by default

Nothing shouts unless something needs you. Alerts appear only when they matter and clear themselves.

### Colour means something

Each thing keeps one colour everywhere. Things glow only while they are active.

### Forgiving touch

Targets are at least 44 px, usually 56–70 px. Risky actions ask for a second tap.

### Summary, then sheet

The home screen summarises. Tapping a card opens a large rounded sheet with the controls.

### Two themes, both real

Dark and light switch at sunset and sunrise. Motion is slow, subtle and respects reduced motion.

